[{"id":"VRCE-2-108-1","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":108,"verse":1,"english":"On Bharata having returned, while Rāma was dwelling in the woods, he noticed affright among the ascetics, added to a desire to remove to another place.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.656,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-116-1"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2108001","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"32e9d0d990137f2983aa918af9728f5648d60d0ef9bb89b8b77c35320b3d6c93","compact":"a5779b652c19eb8288c045d80b4205066db44fe55bfe5ac114899eaa6e3d9c18","nasal":"a5779b652c19eb8288c045d80b4205066db44fe55bfe5ac114899eaa6e3d9c18"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-108-2","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":108,"verse":2,"english":"And those ascetic that were living happily in the asylum in Citrakuța, relying upon Rāma (for their protection), he found to be wrought up with anxiety.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-116-2"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2108002","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"044aacd2e488901e04765aef81ae748112424121b02a1e0be67caef34f454abb","compact":"6f43f77c6957fb37488b83f0cc104e4aad74a03fb2a6b8d1857909a6556568e9","nasal":"6f43f77c6957fb37488b83f0cc104e4aad74a03fb2a6b8d1857909a6556568e9"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-108-3","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":108,"verse":3,"english":"And by means of signs by the eye and contractions of the brow, they, afflicted with fear, were, alluding to Răma, slowly speaking to each other.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.886,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-116-3"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2108003","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"a93e84f51c8738eb90a0e6eff6358ba024a337bb4291ada40212d64